Approach: Character-by-Character Comparison

1. Take each character from the first string.
2. Compare it with the same index in all other strings.
3. If any mismatch occurs, return the prefix built so far.
4. Otherwise add the character to the result.
5. Continue until all characters are checked.

Time Complexity: O(n × m)
Space Complexity: O(1)

Where:
n = number of strings
m = length of shortest string




class Solution:
    def longestCommonPrefix(self, strs: List[str]) -> str:
        result = ""

        for i in range(len(strs[0])):

            ch = strs[0][i]

            for j in range(1, len(strs)):

                if i >= len(strs[j]) or strs[j][i] != ch:
                    return result

            result += ch

        return result
        
